                            <comment id="487134" author="sebastien" created="Tue, 10 Feb 2026 13:42:55 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;This timeout issue in interop testing (server EXA5, client EXA6) started to occur on 02/09/26.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="487328" author="sebastien" created="Wed, 11 Feb 2026 14:33:53 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;According to test results in &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/63923&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/63923&lt;/a&gt; , the patch that is causing this regression is:&lt;br/&gt;
&quot;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19763&quot; title=&quot;Enable TCP zerocopy sending by default&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-19763&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-19763&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; socklnd: Check sendpage_ok for ZC&quot; &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/63535&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/63535&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Note this patch was submitted with the &apos;trivial&apos; keyword.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=xqu&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;xqu&quot;&gt;xqu&lt;/a&gt; could you please:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;alternate&quot; type=&quot;square&quot;&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;push a quick patch to b_es6_0 that skips sanity test_807a in case of interop testing, as this issue is blocking any patch pushed to b_es6_0 at the moment&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;investigate on the reason of the test failure, and possibly find a fix? (did we miss having a connect flag?)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</comment>
                            <comment id="487484" author="JIRAUSER20209" created="Thu, 12 Feb 2026 13:34:05 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Sure, I&apos;ll follow up on this. Thanks!&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="500802" author="adilger" created="Wed, 2 Sep 2026 21:33:35 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=xqu&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;xqu&quot;&gt;xqu&lt;/a&gt; this subtest is still failing in interop testing 6 months after you said you would follow up.  Please investigate.  This seems like a fairly significant interop issue (also affecting 2.15.8 server with 2.17.57 client):&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://testing.whamcloud.com/search?client_branch=master&amp;amp;server_branch=b2_15&amp;amp;horizon=2332800&amp;amp;status%5B%5D=TIMEOUT&amp;amp;test_set_script_id=f9516376-32bc-11e0-aaee-52540025f9ae&amp;amp;sub_test_script_id=0bdbb02a-03e1-4cb3-b7f1-e4c603e63458&amp;amp;source=sub_tests#redirect&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/search?client_branch=master&amp;amp;server_branch=b2_15&amp;amp;horizon=2332800&amp;amp;status%5B%5D=TIMEOUT&amp;amp;test_set_script_id=f9516376-32bc-11e0-aaee-52540025f9ae&amp;amp;sub_test_script_id=0bdbb02a-03e1-4cb3-b7f1-e4c603e63458&amp;amp;source=sub_tests#redirect&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/e7e79f88-b555-4a79-9fc6-0f9a9d1fd879&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/e7e79f88-b555-4a79-9fc6-0f9a9d1fd879&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="500903" author="JIRAUSER20209" created="Thu, 3 Sep 2026 16:23:52 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Hi &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=adilger&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;adilger&quot;&gt;adilger&lt;/a&gt;, sorry about that. I missed this ticket. I&apos;ll start investigating it this week. Thank you!&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="501250" author="JIRAUSER20209" created="Tue, 8 Sep 2026 16:05:34 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;This issue appears to be related to patch &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/63266&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;LU-19763&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/37300&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;LU-12945&lt;/a&gt; disabled the zero-copy feature directly on VMs, based on the rationale that &quot;when running on a hypervisor platform, zero copy buffers may still be referenced when write queue size is zero.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/63266&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;LU-19763&lt;/a&gt; re-enabled zero-copy on VMs by introducing the `sendpage_ok()` check, which brings a significant performance improvement. While `sendpage_ok()` provides some protection against `PageSlab`, it doesn&apos;t seem to fundamentally resolve the issue raised in &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-12945&quot; title=&quot;Avoid sending PageSlab pages through tcp stack&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-12945&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-12945&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Another reason for the `sanity test_807a` timeout is that the `master + b2_15` version combination has NI Recovery issues after send failures.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I&apos;ll run some additional tests locally to gather more information and explore potential approaches to address this issue. Thanks!&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="501942" author="adilger" created="Tue, 22 Sep 2026 07:31:38 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Still failing 6-7 times per week.  &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                    </comments>
